{"schemaVersion":3,"studio":{"samples":[],"profiles":[],"runs":[{"id":"66e2125f-a881-4765-b7b9-028dbe91567e","kind":"draft","sceneId":"44ba1fd1-33a1-4751-8a33-9832632671ef","createdAt":"2026-09-06T07:30:07.823Z","worldRevision":4,"mode":"opening","direction":"Write one short paragraph: Mara waits for a ferry. Under 40 words. Keep all events ordinary.","sceneText":"","start":0,"end":0,"candidate":"Mara, under the watchful eyes of her notebooks, waited for a ferry that would carry her to her destination. As she looked out at the water, she couldn't help but feel a sense of melancholy about the passage of time and the endless journey that had taken her from one place to another. Her notes began with a small sentence: 'Underneath the sea, there are no ships,' and Mara continued her journey, her thoughts wandering through the vast ocean, contemplating life's mysteries.","context":"{\"world\":\"The Quiet Tide\",\"scene\":\"What the water remembers\",\"purpose\":\"\",\"perspective\":\"third\",\"viewpoint\":\"\",\"participants\":[\"be618e79-fef8-46ab-9bfd-69bf785e15a4\",\"d18fd577-00f7-4376-b95e-eba442a722df\"],\"location\":\"\",\"time\":\"\",\"branch\":\"\",\"branchHead\":\"\",\"authorInstructions\":\"Write with specificity and restraint. Leave room for the player to choose. Never decide the player character’s actions or speech.\",\"sceneNotes\":\"Open with a discrepancy small enough to dismiss, and specific enough to remember.\",\"recentBranch\":[],\"before\":\"\",\"after\":\"\"}","sources":[{"id":"be618e79-fef8-46ab-9bfd-69bf785e15a4","kind":"entity","title":"Mara Vale","text":"{\"type\":\"Character\",\"summary\":\"Mara keeps a spare notebook in her coat and writes down the names of passing ships.\",\"visibility\":\"public\"}","writerAllowed":true},{"id":"d8184069-fdd9-49b6-86fe-c05312e302d7","kind":"entity","title":"Ivo Senn","text":"{\"type\":\"Character\",\"summary\":\"The last keeper of the Ninth Lantern. A patient man with salt-white hair, ink-stained fingers, and a habit of answering questions with questions.\",\"visibility\":\"public\"}","writerAllowed":true},{"id":"5f2d33cb-f628-4bf3-930b-a5e4cfaaae19","kind":"entity","title":"Nera Moss","text":"{\"type\":\"Character\",\"summary\":\"A ferryperson who knows every channel through the tidal flats. She remembers the names of everyone who has crossed with her.\",\"visibility\":\"public\"}","writerAllowed":true},{"id":"b0b8d4dc-1128-4042-988f-7f5d31716295","kind":"entity","title":"Bellwether","text":"{\"type\":\"Location\",\"summary\":\"A small town arranged around a horseshoe harbor. At low tide, an old road emerges from the water and leads toward a place absent from every map.\",\"visibility\":\"public\"}","writerAllowed":true},{"id":"d18fd577-00f7-4376-b95e-eba442a722df","kind":"entity","title":"The Ninth Lantern","text":"{\"type\":\"Location\",\"summary\":\"A decommissioned lighthouse on the headland. Its nine windows look toward nine different stretches of sea. Only eight can be seen from outside.\",\"visibility\":\"public\"}","writerAllowed":true},{"id":"e79c6163-7b98-4453-aea6-257140d8251f","kind":"entity","title":"The Tidekeepers","text":"{\"type\":\"Faction\",\"summary\":\"A loose association of navigators, fishers, and keepers. They maintain the channel markers and an archive of everything the sea has returned.\",\"visibility\":\"public\"}","writerAllowed":true},{"id":"34093365-c73d-4447-a671-39f527b52748","kind":"fact","title":"The Ninth Lantern: last lit","text":"{\"subjectId\":\"d18fd577-00f7-4376-b95e-eba442a722df\",\"predicate\":\"last lit\",\"value\":\"Seven years ago, on the night Mara left town.\",\"visibility\":\"public\",\"knownTo\":[]}","writerAllowed":true},{"id":"cd4f6038-345b-4acd-a281-149d5b5b5ca3","kind":"relationship","title":"born in","text":"{\"from\":\"be618e79-fef8-46ab-9bfd-69bf785e15a4\",\"to\":\"b0b8d4dc-1128-4042-988f-7f5d31716295\",\"description\":\"\",\"visibility\":\"public\"}","writerAllowed":true},{"id":"ee6caf1c-cd16-41cd-ae4b-b1af676f0499